1
00:00:01,084 --> 00:00:02,626
<i>- Previously on "The Ark."</i>

2
00:00:02,627 --> 00:00:03,794
- We can't let anyone
know about this.

3
00:00:03,795 --> 00:00:05,713
- Know about what?

4
00:00:05,714 --> 00:00:07,047
- Hey, what's up?
[buzzing]

5
00:00:07,048 --> 00:00:08,424
<i>[panel chimes]</i>

6
00:00:08,425 --> 00:00:09,967
- That took you long
enough.

7
00:00:09,968 --> 00:00:11,135
- [screams]

8
00:00:11,136 --> 00:00:12,469
- I'm gonna move
the slab away from her!

9
00:00:12,470 --> 00:00:14,388
[screams]

10
00:00:14,389 --> 00:00:16,182
Guys, you have to see this.

11
00:00:18,226 --> 00:00:21,645
<i>[tense music]</i>

12
00:00:21,646 --> 00:00:23,355
- I think you need
to take me to med bay.

13
00:00:23,356 --> 00:00:26,191
- What's wrong?
- [stuttering]

14
00:00:26,192 --> 00:00:28,068
I can't--
- OK, OK, OK.

15
00:00:28,069 --> 00:00:29,153
- You can freaking control me.

16
00:00:29,154 --> 00:00:30,195
- [distorted]
Don't try that again.

17
00:00:30,196 --> 00:00:31,447
[normally]
You owe me your life.

18
00:00:31,448 --> 00:00:33,073
You should be thanking me.
- Thank you.

19
00:00:33,074 --> 00:00:35,952
Now please,
get out of my head.

20
00:00:40,081 --> 00:00:42,958
[breathing heavily]

21
00:00:42,959 --> 00:00:44,752
- [chuckles]

22
00:00:44,753 --> 00:00:47,630
Give me the silent treatment
all you want.

23
00:00:56,222 --> 00:00:57,639
- Need a spotter?

24
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:59,016
- I'm OK.

25
00:00:59,017 --> 00:01:00,350
- Good.

26
00:01:00,351 --> 00:01:02,436
You don't need
any distractions.

27
00:01:02,437 --> 00:01:03,521
Now leave.

28
00:01:10,862 --> 00:01:12,696
- You know what?

29
00:01:12,697 --> 00:01:15,366
I do need a spotter.

30
00:01:15,367 --> 00:01:17,284
Just one a wee bit stronger.

31
00:01:17,285 --> 00:01:20,663
<i>[peaceful music]</i>

32
00:01:20,664 --> 00:01:24,708
<i>♪ ♪</i>

33
00:01:24,709 --> 00:01:26,001
Oh?

34
00:01:26,002 --> 00:01:27,795
- How's that for strong?

35
00:01:27,796 --> 00:01:29,797
- I see what you're doing,
and I don't care.

36
00:01:29,798 --> 00:01:32,675
- I admit I was wrong,
and I accept my defeat.

37
00:01:32,676 --> 00:01:35,219
- You're going to have to pay
the price for doubting me.

38
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:37,554
- And what's that then?

39
00:01:37,555 --> 00:01:38,555
- Mm-hmm.

40
00:01:38,556 --> 00:01:45,522
<i>♪ ♪</i>

41
00:01:50,777 --> 00:01:53,904
- [sighs] You know what?

42
00:01:53,905 --> 00:01:55,698
Have your fun while you can.

43
00:01:55,699 --> 00:02:02,454
<i>♪ ♪</i>

44
00:02:02,455 --> 00:02:08,335
Because everything is gonna
change once we get to Homebase.

45
00:02:08,336 --> 00:02:11,005
<i>[tense music]</i>

46
00:02:11,006 --> 00:02:12,464
<i>[monitors beeping]</i>

47
00:02:12,465 --> 00:02:14,842
- You're taking
a million cells?

48
00:02:14,843 --> 00:02:17,177
- Oh, I'm extracting
a lot more than that.

49
00:02:17,178 --> 00:02:20,764
But I only need a million cells
to grow a culture to study it.

50
00:02:20,765 --> 00:02:22,766
OK. You're numbed.

51
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:23,934
Deep breath.

52
00:02:23,935 --> 00:02:26,020
- [inhales deeply]

53
00:02:26,021 --> 00:02:29,481
- I'm pretty sure the cure
for Gen-3 psychosis

54
00:02:29,482 --> 00:02:33,944
has to do with why your GABA
receptor genes don't degrade.

55
00:02:33,945 --> 00:02:38,157
You might feel a small pinch.

56
00:02:38,158 --> 00:02:39,325
- [groans softly]

57
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:44,163
All done.

58
00:02:44,164 --> 00:02:45,498
- Oh.

59
00:02:46,916 --> 00:02:48,876
That wasn't too bad
for a needle to my spine.

60
00:02:48,877 --> 00:02:53,464
- [chuckles] Technically,
it went in your brain stem.

61
00:02:53,465 --> 00:02:54,673
- What's next?
How can I help?

62
00:02:54,674 --> 00:02:56,216
- Well, I was--
- <i>Captain.</i>

63
00:02:56,217 --> 00:02:57,760
<i>We're picking up
a distress call.</i>

64
00:02:57,761 --> 00:02:59,428
<i>It's from "Ark 16."</i>

65
00:02:59,429 --> 00:03:02,848
- Oh, go do captain stuff.
I'll do science stuff.

66
00:03:02,849 --> 00:03:04,141
- You got it.

67
00:03:04,142 --> 00:03:06,977
<i>[soft dramatic music]</i>

68
00:03:06,978 --> 00:03:08,020
Set a course.

69
00:03:08,021 --> 00:03:09,355
I'm on my way
to the bridge now.

70
00:03:09,356 --> 00:03:11,815
[insects droning]

71
00:03:11,816 --> 00:03:13,484
<i>[WD chimes]
- Mr. Strickland?</i>

72
00:03:13,485 --> 00:03:14,485
- Alicia?

73
00:03:14,486 --> 00:03:15,903
<i>- Yes. Good news.</i>

74
00:03:15,904 --> 00:03:20,366
<i>Your name's been cleared.
It's safe to come home.</i>

75
00:03:20,367 --> 00:03:24,870
- Oh, that's a relief.
Thank you.

76
00:03:24,871 --> 00:03:26,372
<i>- Oh, thank Mr. Avega.</i>

77
00:03:26,373 --> 00:03:27,915
<i>He got Lati to trick
Ves into saying--</i>

78
00:03:27,916 --> 00:03:30,793
- Alicia?

79
00:03:30,794 --> 00:03:35,339
You better send
a science team to my location.

80
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:38,175
<i>- What? Why?</i>

81
00:03:38,176 --> 00:03:42,096
- I just found something
strange.

82
00:03:42,097 --> 00:03:45,140
<i>[dramatic music]</i>

83
00:03:45,141 --> 00:03:49,353
<i>♪ ♪</i>

84
00:03:49,354 --> 00:03:52,314
<i>[uplifting music]</i>

85
00:03:52,315 --> 00:03:59,489
<i>♪ ♪</i>

86
00:04:09,332 --> 00:04:11,625
[energy crackling]

87
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:15,754
<i>- I repeat, this is
Captain St. John of "Ark 16."</i>

88
00:04:15,755 --> 00:04:18,215
<i>We are under siege.
Please send help.</i>

89
00:04:18,216 --> 00:04:19,466
<i>I re--</i>

90
00:04:19,467 --> 00:04:21,301
- The message is 31 hours old.

91
00:04:21,302 --> 00:04:23,220
- Then we might still
be able to help.

92
00:04:23,221 --> 00:04:24,430
What do we know?

93
00:04:24,431 --> 00:04:26,223
- "Ark 16" was one
of the last Arks

94
00:04:26,224 --> 00:04:28,016
to launch under GSA command.

95
00:04:28,017 --> 00:04:29,852
- Where are they now?

96
00:04:29,853 --> 00:04:31,437
- Dena-197,

97
00:04:31,438 --> 00:04:34,565
listed in our database
as a colonization candidate.

98
00:04:34,566 --> 00:04:36,942
- Could someone be challenging
them for the planet?

99
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:38,694
- Statistically unlikely.

100
00:04:38,695 --> 00:04:41,155
- Not everyone is as open
to peace as you are, Captain.

101
00:04:41,156 --> 00:04:42,740
- Maybe it's "EF1."

102
00:04:42,741 --> 00:04:44,783
Avega still hasn't been
able to contact them.

103
00:04:44,784 --> 00:04:47,161
- Maybe they missed the memo
that the war is over.

104
00:04:47,162 --> 00:04:49,663
- Or it could also be a trap.

105
00:04:49,664 --> 00:04:51,332
Drake is still
searching for you.

106
00:04:51,333 --> 00:04:53,417
- The thought crossed my mind.

107
00:04:53,418 --> 00:04:55,335
- We're approaching
the coordinates.

108
00:04:55,336 --> 00:04:58,797
Dropping out of FTL
in three, two...

109
00:04:58,798 --> 00:04:59,716
<i>[panel beeps]</i>

110
00:05:02,469 --> 00:05:05,429
<i>[soft suspenseful music]</i>

111
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:06,680
<i>♪ ♪</i>

112
00:05:06,681 --> 00:05:08,932
- Huh.

113
00:05:08,933 --> 00:05:11,268
<i>♪ ♪</i>

114
00:05:11,269 --> 00:05:14,772
- I don't see any evidence
of a colony on the surface.

115
00:05:14,773 --> 00:05:17,107
- I don't detect
other ships in orbit.

116
00:05:17,108 --> 00:05:19,318
- Except "Ark 16."

117
00:05:19,319 --> 00:05:21,445
- It looks undamaged.

118
00:05:21,446 --> 00:05:22,946
- All the systems are
functioning.

119
00:05:22,947 --> 00:05:26,659
There's life signs
for 285 people.

120
00:05:26,660 --> 00:05:28,410
Yeah, I don't see any signs
of an attack.

121
00:05:28,411 --> 00:05:29,620
- Hail them.

122
00:05:29,621 --> 00:05:32,498
- I've been trying to,
but there's no response.

123
00:05:32,499 --> 00:05:34,375
- Can we tap into
their internal cameras?

124
00:05:34,376 --> 00:05:35,876
- They're offline.

125
00:05:35,877 --> 00:05:38,170
- Then the only way we're
getting answers is to go over.

126
00:05:38,171 --> 00:05:39,630
- We should be cautious.

127
00:05:39,631 --> 00:05:41,757
Keep the boarding party small
and armed.

128
00:05:41,758 --> 00:05:43,300
- Agreed.
Shuttle in ten.

129
00:05:43,301 --> 00:05:44,927
Eva, you're with us.

130
00:05:44,928 --> 00:05:46,470
<i>♪ ♪</i>

131
00:05:46,471 --> 00:05:48,972
- So maybe
I should come with you?

132
00:05:48,973 --> 00:05:50,474
- I need you here.

133
00:05:50,475 --> 00:05:53,185
I'm taking Eva, so I need
an engineer on the ship.

134
00:05:53,186 --> 00:05:54,395
- Oh.

135
00:05:54,396 --> 00:05:55,646
Because for a second there,

136
00:05:55,647 --> 00:05:58,107
I thought it was about
professional propriety.

137
00:05:58,108 --> 00:06:00,317
- [chuckles]

138
00:06:00,318 --> 00:06:02,319
<i>♪ ♪</i>

139
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,655
Um--

140
00:06:04,656 --> 00:06:06,323
it wasn't, but now it is.

141
00:06:06,324 --> 00:06:11,120
<i>♪ ♪</i>

142
00:06:11,121 --> 00:06:12,287
- [sighs]

143
00:06:12,288 --> 00:06:16,667
<i>♪ ♪</i>

144
00:06:16,668 --> 00:06:19,796
[metallic clanking]

145
00:06:28,471 --> 00:06:31,932
- There's an unknown
contaminant in the air.

146
00:06:31,933 --> 00:06:33,267
I'll take a sample.

147
00:06:33,268 --> 00:06:35,310
- Copy that.
Helmets stay on.

148
00:06:35,311 --> 00:06:37,271
<i>♪ ♪</i>

149
00:06:37,272 --> 00:06:38,939
<i>[panel beeping]</i>

150
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:45,322
<i>♪ ♪</i>

151
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:48,574
- Why are the bulkheads closed?

152
00:06:48,575 --> 00:06:51,076
This seems off, right?

153
00:06:51,077 --> 00:06:52,202
- Little bit.

154
00:06:52,203 --> 00:06:55,330
Can you do a sweep
with Hendricks and Wilson?

155
00:06:55,331 --> 00:06:56,498
Eva, see if you can

156
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:58,042
pull anything off
the internal feeds.

157
00:06:58,043 --> 00:07:01,462
<i>♪ ♪</i>

158
00:07:01,463 --> 00:07:04,381
<i>[tense music]</i>

159
00:07:04,382 --> 00:07:05,592
<i>♪ ♪</i>

160
00:07:09,054 --> 00:07:10,345
- So

161
00:07:10,346 --> 00:07:14,141
you and Ian finally decided
to go for it in real life?

162
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:15,934
- It's that obvious?

163
00:07:15,935 --> 00:07:17,311
- Pretty much.

164
00:07:17,312 --> 00:07:20,230
<i>[panel chiming]</i>

165
00:07:20,231 --> 00:07:22,650
- Can I ask you a question?

166
00:07:22,651 --> 00:07:26,070
How do you and Brice draw
professional boundaries?

167
00:07:26,071 --> 00:07:27,404
- Boundaries?

168
00:07:27,405 --> 00:07:30,324
Good thing you didn't walk
in on us earlier in the gym.

169
00:07:30,325 --> 00:07:31,450
- [chuckles softly]

170
00:07:31,451 --> 00:07:34,746
<i>[panel chiming]</i>

171
00:07:35,372 --> 00:07:36,497
I'm in.

172
00:07:36,498 --> 00:07:37,915
Half the bulkheads
are in lockdown.

173
00:07:37,916 --> 00:07:39,958
Most of the WD signatures
I'm detecting

174
00:07:39,959 --> 00:07:41,335
are behind the lockdowns.

175
00:07:41,336 --> 00:07:46,048
- So they're either locked in
or keeping something out.

176
00:07:46,049 --> 00:07:47,549
- Get away from me!

177
00:07:47,550 --> 00:07:49,134
- Follow me.

178
00:07:49,135 --> 00:07:52,054
<i>[tense music]</i>

179
00:07:52,055 --> 00:07:53,347
<i>♪ ♪</i>

180
00:07:53,348 --> 00:07:54,556
- Get away from me!

181
00:07:54,557 --> 00:07:56,892
- Hey, stop!
What are you doing? Hey!

182
00:07:56,893 --> 00:07:58,769
<i>♪ ♪</i>

183
00:07:58,770 --> 00:08:00,729
- He slept with my wife!

184
00:08:00,730 --> 00:08:03,190
- You don't even have a wife.

185
00:08:03,191 --> 00:08:05,067
- [snarls]

186
00:08:05,068 --> 00:08:07,194
- Wait!

187
00:08:07,195 --> 00:08:08,612
<i>- Kimi to Garnet.</i>

188
00:08:08,613 --> 00:08:12,282
<i>You better come
to the Mess Hall.</i>

189
00:08:12,283 --> 00:08:13,325
- Come on.

190
00:08:13,326 --> 00:08:15,911
<i>[tense music]</i>

191
00:08:15,912 --> 00:08:17,121
<i>♪ ♪</i>

192
00:08:17,122 --> 00:08:20,249
What happened?

193
00:08:20,250 --> 00:08:22,626
- They all have
some sort of skin condition.

194
00:08:22,627 --> 00:08:24,503
- Must be an infection
or some sort of poisoning

195
00:08:24,504 --> 00:08:26,505
from the contaminant
we detected.

196
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:29,341
- But we just saw
two crew that have it.

197
00:08:29,342 --> 00:08:30,676
They were alive.

198
00:08:30,677 --> 00:08:33,887
- These people didn't die
from an infection.

199
00:08:33,888 --> 00:08:37,099
This woman's head
is smashed in.

200
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:40,477
<i>♪ ♪</i>

201
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:41,979
This man was stabbed.

202
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:45,065
<i>♪ ♪</i>

203
00:08:45,066 --> 00:08:48,944
- I think this person
was strangled.

204
00:08:48,945 --> 00:08:51,280
These people killed each other.

205
00:08:51,281 --> 00:08:53,490
<i>♪ ♪</i>

206
00:08:53,491 --> 00:08:55,993
[electricity zapping]

207
00:08:55,994 --> 00:08:57,619
Stop!
You're killing him!

208
00:08:57,620 --> 00:09:00,372
- My first officer mutinied.

209
00:09:00,373 --> 00:09:01,665
[electricity crackling]

210
00:09:01,666 --> 00:09:03,042
I can't allow that.

211
00:09:03,043 --> 00:09:04,668
- What's on the back
of your hand, Captain?

212
00:09:04,669 --> 00:09:09,506
<i>♪ ♪</i>

213
00:09:09,507 --> 00:09:10,883
- Who are you?

214
00:09:10,884 --> 00:09:13,594
- Captain Sharon Garnet.
We're from "Ark 1."

215
00:09:13,595 --> 00:09:14,887
- You boarded
without permission.

216
00:09:14,888 --> 00:09:17,181
- We were answering
your distress call.

217
00:09:17,182 --> 00:09:18,182
What happened here?

218
00:09:18,183 --> 00:09:19,516
- You want to take my ship?

219
00:09:19,517 --> 00:09:21,769
- We're here to help you.

220
00:09:21,770 --> 00:09:23,687
- Sir, you need
to step back now!

221
00:09:23,688 --> 00:09:26,315
<i>♪ ♪</i>

222
00:09:26,316 --> 00:09:27,858
<i>[device beeps, alarm blaring]</i>

223
00:09:27,859 --> 00:09:29,652
- This is Captain
to anyone still loyal.

224
00:09:29,653 --> 00:09:31,362
We have intruders.

225
00:09:31,363 --> 00:09:33,030
Do not let them escape!

226
00:09:33,031 --> 00:09:34,698
- Sharon?
- Back to the shuttle.

227
00:09:34,699 --> 00:09:36,367
We'll figure this out
from "Ark 1."

228
00:09:36,368 --> 00:09:37,993
Go. Go.

229
00:09:37,994 --> 00:09:43,916
<i>♪ ♪</i>

230
00:09:43,917 --> 00:09:46,210
Come on!
<i>[alarm blaring]</i>

231
00:09:46,211 --> 00:09:52,383
<i>♪ ♪</i>

232
00:09:52,384 --> 00:09:54,259
The less contact, the better.

233
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:55,552
Run!

234
00:09:55,553 --> 00:09:58,472
[shouting and grunting]

235
00:09:58,473 --> 00:10:05,521
<i>♪ ♪</i>

236
00:10:05,522 --> 00:10:07,481
[Eva yelps]

237
00:10:07,482 --> 00:10:13,362
<i>♪ ♪</i>

238
00:10:13,363 --> 00:10:14,738
- Kimi!
Come on.

239
00:10:14,739 --> 00:10:16,615
Go.
Go, go, go!

240
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:18,284
Come on, Eva!

241
00:10:20,120 --> 00:10:21,787
Hurry!

242
00:10:21,788 --> 00:10:24,748
[crew shouting]

243
00:10:24,749 --> 00:10:27,584
<i>♪ ♪</i>

244
00:10:27,585 --> 00:10:31,088
[people thudding against door]

245
00:10:31,089 --> 00:10:33,048
<i>- Decontamination protocol.</i>

246
00:10:33,049 --> 00:10:37,177
<i>Clear in five, four,
three, two, one.</i>

247
00:10:37,178 --> 00:10:38,429
<i>[panel beeps]</i>

248
00:10:38,430 --> 00:10:41,473
- The air is free
of contaminants.

249
00:10:41,474 --> 00:10:44,768
- Let's go before they get
in here and recontaminate.

250
00:10:44,769 --> 00:10:50,941
<i>♪ ♪</i>

251
00:10:50,942 --> 00:10:52,652
Kimi, get us out of here.

252
00:11:00,869 --> 00:11:02,244
<i>[panel chimes]</i>

253
00:11:02,245 --> 00:11:05,290
- It's safe for everyone
to take off their helmets.

254
00:11:09,836 --> 00:11:11,962
- Is everyone OK?

255
00:11:11,963 --> 00:11:13,339
- Yeah.
- Good.

256
00:11:13,340 --> 00:11:14,965
First order of business
when we get to "Ark 1,"

257
00:11:14,966 --> 00:11:16,467
figure out how
to help those people

258
00:11:16,468 --> 00:11:17,927
before they kill each other.

259
00:11:21,848 --> 00:11:24,934
<i>[ominous music]</i>

260
00:11:29,397 --> 00:11:31,231
<i>[faint beeping]</i>

261
00:11:31,232 --> 00:11:33,484
- It's OK.
I'm fine.

262
00:11:33,485 --> 00:11:36,779
- Yeah, I'll be
the judge of that.

263
00:11:36,780 --> 00:11:40,282
Pupil dilation, normal.
Autonomic responses are good.

264
00:11:40,283 --> 00:11:43,661
And you have no residual pain?

265
00:11:43,662 --> 00:11:45,079
- I don't even have a headache.

266
00:11:45,080 --> 00:11:46,872
- Seriously?

267
00:11:46,873 --> 00:11:49,792
You were screaming when
that thing electrocuted you.

268
00:11:49,793 --> 00:11:51,752
- Has the object been dormant
since it attacked Kelly?

269
00:11:51,753 --> 00:11:53,045
- Yeah.

270
00:11:53,046 --> 00:11:56,673
- But only after half of it
changed to English.

271
00:11:56,674 --> 00:11:58,842
- That would explain
the results I got

272
00:11:58,843 --> 00:12:01,095
from a diagnostic I ran
on Kelly's implants.

273
00:12:01,096 --> 00:12:03,055
It looks like
your brain's CPU

274
00:12:03,056 --> 00:12:06,225
sent out a massive data signal
when you were shocked.

275
00:12:06,226 --> 00:12:08,936
I wonder if somehow
your augmentations connected

276
00:12:08,937 --> 00:12:11,605
to the slab and triggered
a reverse subcarrier wave.

277
00:12:11,606 --> 00:12:13,315
- I love you, but sometimes

278
00:12:13,316 --> 00:12:15,526
I don't understand the words
that come out of your mouth.

279
00:12:15,527 --> 00:12:18,445
- I think the slab
learned English from Kelly

280
00:12:18,446 --> 00:12:19,780
through her implants.

281
00:12:19,781 --> 00:12:23,742
Like it copied a whole language
from her brain.

282
00:12:23,743 --> 00:12:26,120
- So it's just lucky
we have a post-human

283
00:12:26,121 --> 00:12:28,247
that can connect with
the technology in this lab?

284
00:12:28,248 --> 00:12:30,708
- Or the people from the cave
discovered your implants

285
00:12:30,709 --> 00:12:32,626
when you were their prisoner.

286
00:12:32,627 --> 00:12:35,379
- Wait, does that mean
that the triangle device

287
00:12:35,380 --> 00:12:39,216
that activated the slab was
left specifically for Kelly?

288
00:12:39,217 --> 00:12:40,884
- So you think I was targeted?

289
00:12:40,885 --> 00:12:42,302
- Or chosen.

290
00:12:42,303 --> 00:12:45,305
<i>[tense music]</i>

291
00:12:45,306 --> 00:12:47,057
<i>♪ ♪</i>

292
00:12:47,058 --> 00:12:49,184
[indistinct chatter]

293
00:12:49,185 --> 00:12:52,896
- Thank you for helping
prove my innocence, Zed.

294
00:12:52,897 --> 00:12:57,651
- We stand together
or we fall alone.

295
00:12:57,652 --> 00:13:02,322
I gave Lati work release
in exchange for her aid,

296
00:13:02,323 --> 00:13:05,367
but she's worried
about retribution.

297
00:13:05,368 --> 00:13:06,660
- I don't blame her.

298
00:13:06,661 --> 00:13:08,620
We don't know who among us
is Black Thorn

299
00:13:08,621 --> 00:13:11,081
and still loyal to Ves.

300
00:13:11,082 --> 00:13:15,335
- Including some people
working in security.

301
00:13:15,336 --> 00:13:18,964
- Anyone on "Ark 11"
is a suspect.

302
00:13:18,965 --> 00:13:22,092
- Just because they aren't
from "Ark 11"

303
00:13:22,093 --> 00:13:24,511
doesn't preclude them
from being part

304
00:13:24,512 --> 00:13:27,014
of another Black Thorn unit.

305
00:13:27,015 --> 00:13:28,098
- So what are you saying?

306
00:13:28,099 --> 00:13:29,767
We can't trust any
former GSA members

307
00:13:29,768 --> 00:13:31,060
of the security team?

308
00:13:31,061 --> 00:13:35,314
- What I'm saying is
we don't know if we can.

309
00:13:35,315 --> 00:13:38,108
Which is why I'd like to

310
00:13:38,109 --> 00:13:42,196
put a former EF security man
in charge.

311
00:13:42,197 --> 00:13:43,781
- Agreed.

312
00:13:43,782 --> 00:13:46,617
On an interim basis until
we round up Ves and her team.

313
00:13:46,618 --> 00:13:48,952
<i>[WD beeps]</i>

314
00:13:48,953 --> 00:13:50,079
<i>- Trust to Felix.</i>

315
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:51,580
<i>I'm studying this
object you found</i>

316
00:13:51,581 --> 00:13:53,832
<i>and, well, it'll be
easier to explain</i>

317
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:55,710
<i>if you just come
back out here.</i>

318
00:13:57,462 --> 00:13:58,963
- Divide and conquer?

319
00:14:03,927 --> 00:14:06,428
[birds singing]

320
00:14:06,429 --> 00:14:07,805
- Well, this is quite
the puzzle

321
00:14:07,806 --> 00:14:10,391
you've discovered here, Felix.

322
00:14:10,392 --> 00:14:12,101
Look at the scorching.

323
00:14:12,102 --> 00:14:15,729
Look how the ground
is disturbed.

324
00:14:15,730 --> 00:14:18,232
This is an impact radius.

325
00:14:18,233 --> 00:14:19,733
- It fell from the sky?

326
00:14:19,734 --> 00:14:22,152
- I think this fell from orbit.

327
00:14:22,153 --> 00:14:24,822
This appears to be part
of a piece of machinery

328
00:14:24,823 --> 00:14:26,907
that fused under
the heat of reentry.

329
00:14:26,908 --> 00:14:29,326
- It's debris.
From what?

330
00:14:29,327 --> 00:14:30,661
- Too damaged to tell.

331
00:14:30,662 --> 00:14:33,122
All I do know is
that it's not ours.

332
00:14:33,123 --> 00:14:34,748
- It's not from
something in orbit?

333
00:14:34,749 --> 00:14:36,834
EF2 or one of those
fore-section bulbs?

334
00:14:36,835 --> 00:14:38,252
- No, they're all intact.
I checked.

335
00:14:38,253 --> 00:14:42,756
This has been here for
at least a year, maybe more.

336
00:14:42,757 --> 00:14:44,925
- How can you be sure?

337
00:14:44,926 --> 00:14:48,804
- Well, the trees are scorched,
but we're still in the shade.

338
00:14:48,805 --> 00:14:51,724
This has been here long enough
for the canopy to regrow.

339
00:14:51,725 --> 00:14:55,686
- That explains why
we never saw it in flyovers.

340
00:14:55,687 --> 00:14:58,480
- Mr. Trust, we found
more debris to the east.

341
00:14:58,481 --> 00:15:00,441
Like, a lot more.

342
00:15:00,442 --> 00:15:03,444
<i>[tense music]</i>

343
00:15:03,445 --> 00:15:05,112
<i>♪ ♪</i>

344
00:15:05,113 --> 00:15:08,282
- Ladies and gentlemen,
let me introduce to you

345
00:15:08,283 --> 00:15:10,617
Mr. Raymond Quinn.

346
00:15:10,618 --> 00:15:14,621
With the unfortunate death
of Mr. Petrovic,

347
00:15:14,622 --> 00:15:18,375
Mr. Quinn will be taking
command of security for now.

348
00:15:18,376 --> 00:15:21,587
- He picks an EF guy.

349
00:15:21,588 --> 00:15:23,798
Big surprise.

350
00:15:31,097 --> 00:15:33,140
- Erica, is it?

351
00:15:33,141 --> 00:15:35,517
- Yes, sir.

352
00:15:35,518 --> 00:15:40,439
- I appointed
a man I served with

353
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:43,150
because I know I can trust him.

354
00:15:43,151 --> 00:15:47,529
- Of course, sir.

355
00:15:47,530 --> 00:15:52,034
- Does anyone else
have an opinion?

356
00:15:52,035 --> 00:15:53,244
Dismissed.

357
00:16:02,253 --> 00:16:06,882
There are still unidentified
Black Thorn members.

358
00:16:06,883 --> 00:16:09,968
Some of them could
be among your men.

359
00:16:09,969 --> 00:16:14,181
- So why don't we just relieve
all the former GSA of duty?

360
00:16:14,182 --> 00:16:18,018
- Because it's easier to
catch a rat inside your house

361
00:16:18,019 --> 00:16:19,770
rather than out.

362
00:16:19,771 --> 00:16:22,731
<i>[suspenseful music]</i>

363
00:16:22,732 --> 00:16:29,864
<i>♪ ♪</i>

364
00:16:46,756 --> 00:16:49,800
<i>[dramatic music]</i>

365
00:16:49,801 --> 00:16:54,055
<i>♪ ♪</i>

366
00:16:56,224 --> 00:16:58,600
[metallic clanking]

367
00:16:58,601 --> 00:17:00,477
- We can't help "Ark 16"
until we figure out

368
00:17:00,478 --> 00:17:02,521
what that contaminant is
and where it came from.

369
00:17:02,522 --> 00:17:04,356
- Well, if they were scouting
the planet to settle,

370
00:17:04,357 --> 00:17:06,734
the pre-colonization team could
have picked it up down there.

371
00:17:06,735 --> 00:17:08,027
[door opens]

372
00:17:08,028 --> 00:17:09,528
- Sorry I'm late.

373
00:17:09,529 --> 00:17:11,488
I've been analyzing the
air sample you brought back.

374
00:17:11,489 --> 00:17:12,865
- What's the verdict?
- Not good.

375
00:17:12,866 --> 00:17:15,617
The particulate replicates
at an extremely high rate.

376
00:17:15,618 --> 00:17:18,245
The rash you described
in the "Ark 16" crew

377
00:17:18,246 --> 00:17:19,705
is likely a histamine reaction.

378
00:17:19,706 --> 00:17:21,999
- So it's a virus.
- No, it's not viral.

379
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:24,626
It's also not
bacterial or parasitic.

380
00:17:24,627 --> 00:17:26,754
It--it behaves in ways
I don't understand.

381
00:17:26,755 --> 00:17:27,838
- Can you stop it?

382
00:17:27,839 --> 00:17:29,256
- Not until I run more tests

383
00:17:29,257 --> 00:17:30,424
and figure out
exactly what it is.

384
00:17:30,425 --> 00:17:31,550
- We don't have time to wait.

385
00:17:31,551 --> 00:17:33,427
The "Ark 16" crew is
at each other's throats.

386
00:17:33,428 --> 00:17:35,220
- Some of them have
already killed each other.

387
00:17:35,221 --> 00:17:37,222
Can we sedate them until
Doc Kabir figures out a cure?

388
00:17:37,223 --> 00:17:38,766
- Not remotely.

389
00:17:38,767 --> 00:17:39,808
- I could take a squad over,

390
00:17:39,809 --> 00:17:41,018
put a sedative
into their system.

391
00:17:41,019 --> 00:17:42,269
- Good idea.

392
00:17:42,270 --> 00:17:43,979
Keep the team small.
Make sure you're armed.

393
00:17:43,980 --> 00:17:45,482
- I'll work on
an insertion plan.

394
00:17:47,275 --> 00:17:50,444
<i>[soft suspenseful music]</i>

395
00:17:50,445 --> 00:17:54,198
<i>♪ ♪</i>

396
00:17:54,199 --> 00:17:56,700
- Once we get to your planet,

397
00:17:56,701 --> 00:17:58,035
you're going to do
as you're told.

398
00:17:58,036 --> 00:18:01,288
- [grunts] Or what?

399
00:18:01,289 --> 00:18:03,165
It's not like you can
actually do anything to me,

400
00:18:03,166 --> 00:18:05,042
as far as I can see.

401
00:18:05,043 --> 00:18:07,711
Other than give me a migraine.

402
00:18:07,712 --> 00:18:10,047
That being said, it's a
pretty big friggin' migraine,

403
00:18:10,048 --> 00:18:11,840
the way you just go on and on.

404
00:18:11,841 --> 00:18:14,593
[door thuds]
What?

405
00:18:14,594 --> 00:18:16,261
Sorry.

406
00:18:16,262 --> 00:18:17,930
Baby, sorry, I was
lost in thought there.

407
00:18:17,931 --> 00:18:19,390
- I left my data pad here.

408
00:18:19,391 --> 00:18:21,100
- Hey, wait, wait, wait, wait.

409
00:18:21,101 --> 00:18:23,227
You mad at me?

410
00:18:23,228 --> 00:18:25,062
- I was attacked on a mission

411
00:18:25,063 --> 00:18:26,897
and you didn't even meet me
at the airlock.

412
00:18:26,898 --> 00:18:29,483
- [sighs]

413
00:18:29,484 --> 00:18:31,068
I'm sorry.

414
00:18:31,069 --> 00:18:33,404
Baby, I'm sorry.
I got distracted. I'm an ass.

415
00:18:33,405 --> 00:18:36,323
- You've been acting strange,
and now I know why.

416
00:18:36,324 --> 00:18:38,909
- Well--[scoffs]
Yeah, because I--I died.

417
00:18:38,910 --> 00:18:40,411
- Don't use that as an excuse.

418
00:18:40,412 --> 00:18:42,204
This started when
you left Homebase.

419
00:18:42,205 --> 00:18:44,790
- What started?
- Cheating on me.

420
00:18:44,791 --> 00:18:47,042
- Cheating on you? What--
what are you talking about?

421
00:18:47,043 --> 00:18:49,086
- With Kimi.

422
00:18:49,087 --> 00:18:49,962
- Are you being
serious right now?

423
00:18:49,963 --> 00:18:51,171
- Yes.

424
00:18:51,172 --> 00:18:52,256
- Do you not remember
a few months ago

425
00:18:52,257 --> 00:18:54,258
when she literally
wanted me dead?

426
00:18:54,259 --> 00:18:56,093
- She wanted you dead because
she was in love with you.

427
00:18:56,094 --> 00:18:57,261
- What?

428
00:18:57,262 --> 00:18:58,429
[laughing] Oh, my God.

429
00:18:58,430 --> 00:18:59,972
- Don't make fun of me!

430
00:18:59,973 --> 00:19:02,224
<i>[ominous music]</i>

431
00:19:02,225 --> 00:19:04,601
- What the hell is that?

432
00:19:04,602 --> 00:19:06,770
- Nothing.

433
00:19:06,771 --> 00:19:08,689
And it's certainly none
of your damn business.

434
00:19:08,690 --> 00:19:11,900
<i>♪ ♪</i>

435
00:19:11,901 --> 00:19:12,943
- [scoffs]

436
00:19:12,944 --> 00:19:14,737
<i>♪ ♪</i>

437
00:19:14,738 --> 00:19:17,114
- Wow.

438
00:19:17,115 --> 00:19:18,283
<i>♪ ♪</i>

439
00:19:22,037 --> 00:19:23,579
[keyboard clacking]

440
00:19:23,580 --> 00:19:25,998
<i>[monitor beeps]</i>

441
00:19:25,999 --> 00:19:27,708
[knock at door]

442
00:19:27,709 --> 00:19:28,793
[door clacks]

443
00:19:29,961 --> 00:19:31,128
- You got a minute?

444
00:19:31,129 --> 00:19:32,546
- Yeah, I'm just waiting

445
00:19:32,547 --> 00:19:36,717
for Kimi's insertion plan
for "Ark 16."

446
00:19:36,718 --> 00:19:38,218
- Listen, sorry if
I was a little pushy

447
00:19:38,219 --> 00:19:40,554
about coming on the mission.

448
00:19:40,555 --> 00:19:43,599
Oh, and for being charming
in public.

449
00:19:43,600 --> 00:19:46,852
I promise to maintain
professional propriety.

450
00:19:46,853 --> 00:19:51,899
Although some of that is on you
resisting this handsome face.

451
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:53,734
- I knew it.

452
00:19:53,735 --> 00:19:56,904
You don't actually
want to be with me.

453
00:19:56,905 --> 00:19:58,072
- Wait.

454
00:19:58,073 --> 00:19:59,156
That's not at all what I meant.

455
00:19:59,157 --> 00:20:00,866
- I know what you meant.

456
00:20:00,867 --> 00:20:03,410
OK?

457
00:20:03,411 --> 00:20:07,206
You don't have any
real feelings for me.

458
00:20:07,207 --> 00:20:08,499
- I'm confused.

459
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:10,584
Where's this coming from?

460
00:20:10,585 --> 00:20:14,088
- No one can ever love me.
I'm a Gen-3 freak.

461
00:20:14,089 --> 00:20:16,840
- I don't think that at all.
No one thinks that.

462
00:20:16,841 --> 00:20:19,843
<i>[suspenseful music]</i>

463
00:20:19,844 --> 00:20:23,889
<i>♪ ♪</i>

464
00:20:23,890 --> 00:20:26,850
- The real question is...

465
00:20:26,851 --> 00:20:31,146
why are you pretending
to be in love with me?

466
00:20:31,147 --> 00:20:32,523
- Can we rewind for a second?

467
00:20:32,524 --> 00:20:33,941
I just came by with a gift.

468
00:20:33,942 --> 00:20:35,734
<i>♪ ♪</i>

469
00:20:35,735 --> 00:20:38,862
- Pull that weapon,
and I'll snap your neck.

470
00:20:38,863 --> 00:20:41,031
- I brought you
a cookie from Mess.

471
00:20:41,032 --> 00:20:42,700
[breathing heavily]

472
00:20:42,701 --> 00:20:47,746
<i>♪ ♪</i>

473
00:20:47,747 --> 00:20:51,667
It's peanut butter chocolate
ch--

474
00:20:51,668 --> 00:20:53,419
chip.

475
00:20:53,420 --> 00:20:55,045
- You think I'm an idiot?

476
00:20:55,046 --> 00:20:57,172
I know it's poisoned.

477
00:20:57,173 --> 00:20:58,966
[grunts]
- [groans softly]

478
00:20:58,967 --> 00:21:01,385
OK.

479
00:21:01,386 --> 00:21:04,180
I think we need
to go see Dr. Kabir.

480
00:21:06,224 --> 00:21:09,977
- You're not going anywhere.

481
00:21:09,978 --> 00:21:11,896
<i>♪ ♪</i>

482
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:18,235
[keyboard clacking]

483
00:21:18,236 --> 00:21:19,529
- [sighs]

484
00:21:28,288 --> 00:21:31,248
<i>[tense music]</i>

485
00:21:31,249 --> 00:21:38,423
<i>♪ ♪</i>

486
00:21:41,968 --> 00:21:43,344
- Hey!

487
00:21:43,345 --> 00:21:44,928
What were you doing in
the server room, Novak?

488
00:21:44,929 --> 00:21:46,931
- Maintenance.
Why?

489
00:21:47,891 --> 00:21:49,016
[groans]

490
00:21:49,017 --> 00:21:50,601
What the hell, Kimi?

491
00:21:50,602 --> 00:21:51,769
That hurt.

492
00:21:51,770 --> 00:21:53,187
- You're an EF spy.

493
00:21:53,188 --> 00:21:57,191
<i>♪ ♪</i>

494
00:21:57,192 --> 00:21:59,151
- I don't want to fight you.

495
00:21:59,152 --> 00:22:01,529
- Oh, it's not
gonna be a fight.

496
00:22:07,118 --> 00:22:09,328
- The test results
for the "Ark 16" air samples.

497
00:22:09,329 --> 00:22:10,996
- Oh, great.
Thank you.

498
00:22:10,997 --> 00:22:13,123
Huh, interesting.

499
00:22:13,124 --> 00:22:14,959
It's behaving more
like a protozoan.

500
00:22:18,296 --> 00:22:20,130
We were looking at it wrong.

501
00:22:20,131 --> 00:22:22,841
The infection isn't caused
by an airborne pathogen.

502
00:22:22,842 --> 00:22:25,219
It's caused by
an airborne spore.

503
00:22:25,220 --> 00:22:26,804
- Like a fungus.

504
00:22:26,805 --> 00:22:29,640
- So it settles on the skin
and releases an ergot alkaloid

505
00:22:29,641 --> 00:22:33,394
that must affect dopamine
and cortisol levels.

506
00:22:33,395 --> 00:22:37,022
The rash isn't the byproduct
of the infection.

507
00:22:37,023 --> 00:22:38,232
It's the cause.

508
00:22:38,233 --> 00:22:43,862
Kabir to Garnet.
I have to find her.

509
00:22:43,863 --> 00:22:46,824
<i>[tense music]</i>

510
00:22:46,825 --> 00:22:47,866
<i>♪ ♪</i>

511
00:22:47,867 --> 00:22:50,035
<i>[dramatic music]</i>

512
00:22:50,036 --> 00:22:52,079
- Clear the way!
- [gasps]

513
00:22:52,080 --> 00:22:53,664
Kimi, what is going on?

514
00:22:53,665 --> 00:22:55,249
- We have to get
this spy to the brig.

515
00:22:55,250 --> 00:22:57,292
<i>♪ ♪</i>

516
00:22:57,293 --> 00:23:00,005
- The infection is on "Ark 1."

517
00:23:02,090 --> 00:23:04,341
[birds singing]

518
00:23:04,342 --> 00:23:06,344
[keyboard clacking]

519
00:23:09,222 --> 00:23:11,682
- I drew this and this

520
00:23:11,683 --> 00:23:15,353
and this and this
and this and this.

521
00:23:17,147 --> 00:23:18,480
- Why?

522
00:23:18,481 --> 00:23:20,274
- I have no idea,

523
00:23:20,275 --> 00:23:22,985
because I drew them
all in my sleep.

524
00:23:22,986 --> 00:23:25,404
I took a nap,
and I woke up on the floor,

525
00:23:25,405 --> 00:23:29,992
surrounded by pages
of whatever this is.

526
00:23:29,993 --> 00:23:35,289
- You did all of this
in your sleep?

527
00:23:35,290 --> 00:23:36,624
- Yeah.

528
00:23:39,544 --> 00:23:41,962
- This sounds like
automatic writing.

529
00:23:41,963 --> 00:23:46,592
But there's no scientific proof
such a thing really exists.

530
00:23:46,593 --> 00:23:48,720
- I would say it really exists.

531
00:23:51,139 --> 00:23:52,390
<i>[beeping]</i>

532
00:23:54,392 --> 00:23:57,644
- Your implants seem
to be functioning properly.

533
00:23:57,645 --> 00:23:59,521
- There's nothing
wrong with them?

534
00:23:59,522 --> 00:24:02,149
- Well, I didn't say that.

535
00:24:02,150 --> 00:24:04,401
This lab obviously did
something to you.

536
00:24:04,402 --> 00:24:06,487
We just can't detect it.

537
00:24:06,488 --> 00:24:09,490
<i>[suspenseful music]</i>

538
00:24:09,491 --> 00:24:14,870
<i>♪ ♪</i>

539
00:24:14,871 --> 00:24:18,415
<i>[radar beeping]</i>

540
00:24:18,416 --> 00:24:21,543
- I'm detecting more debris.

541
00:24:21,544 --> 00:24:24,797
- Why haven't we found
any of this before now?

542
00:24:24,798 --> 00:24:26,298
- Because we never knew
to scan for it.

543
00:24:26,299 --> 00:24:27,716
- And the tree canopy's
too thick

544
00:24:27,717 --> 00:24:29,510
to get a visual
from this height.

545
00:24:29,511 --> 00:24:31,345
<i>♪ ♪</i>

546
00:24:31,346 --> 00:24:33,597
<i>[three beeps]</i>

547
00:24:33,598 --> 00:24:36,350
<i>♪ ♪</i>

548
00:24:36,351 --> 00:24:37,601
- It's all on one line.

549
00:24:37,602 --> 00:24:39,520
- Which means it must have
been one large object

550
00:24:39,521 --> 00:24:43,315
which broke apart in the upper
atmosphere leaving this trail.

551
00:24:43,316 --> 00:24:45,818
- What is it?

552
00:24:45,819 --> 00:24:48,946
<i>[three beeps]</i>

553
00:24:48,947 --> 00:24:50,739
<i>♪ ♪</i>

554
00:24:50,740 --> 00:24:51,699
<i>[two beeps]</i>
- Uh-huh.

555
00:24:51,700 --> 00:24:52,741
- What?

556
00:24:52,742 --> 00:24:54,202
- Trail stops here.

557
00:24:56,287 --> 00:24:58,497
So it's possible that
whatever it was,

558
00:24:58,498 --> 00:25:01,834
the bulk of it lies
at the bottom of this lake.

559
00:25:01,835 --> 00:25:04,628
- I'll take us lower.

560
00:25:04,629 --> 00:25:06,714
- And I'll run LiDAR scans.

561
00:25:06,715 --> 00:25:08,340
If there is
something down there,

562
00:25:08,341 --> 00:25:10,884
I might be able
to assemble an image.

563
00:25:10,885 --> 00:25:18,018
<i>♪ ♪</i>

564
00:25:27,861 --> 00:25:29,236
- I don't see it on here.

565
00:25:29,237 --> 00:25:30,654
- Me neither.

566
00:25:30,655 --> 00:25:32,573
- Well, stylistically,
they're similar.

567
00:25:32,574 --> 00:25:33,782
- Very similar.

568
00:25:33,783 --> 00:25:35,367
- What's similar?

569
00:25:35,368 --> 00:25:37,202
- We're not seeing a match
for what you drew here.

570
00:25:37,203 --> 00:25:38,871
But it's the same
as the symbol--

571
00:25:38,872 --> 00:25:41,373
- I don't understand.

572
00:25:41,374 --> 00:25:44,251
- We're pretty sure that
the symbols on here represent

573
00:25:44,252 --> 00:25:46,920
the language of the people
who abducted you and Angus.

574
00:25:46,921 --> 00:25:49,673
- No, I mean, what symbols?

575
00:25:49,674 --> 00:25:53,218
That thing is all in English.

576
00:25:53,219 --> 00:25:55,763
- Half of this is English.

577
00:25:55,764 --> 00:25:57,514
- All of it is English.

578
00:25:57,515 --> 00:26:00,351
<i>[suspenseful music]</i>

579
00:26:00,352 --> 00:26:01,393
<i>♪ ♪</i>

580
00:26:01,394 --> 00:26:05,272
- Are you saying
you can read this?

581
00:26:05,273 --> 00:26:08,025
- Of course.

582
00:26:08,026 --> 00:26:10,652
It says the same thing
on both sides.

583
00:26:10,653 --> 00:26:13,447
Or almost the same.

584
00:26:13,448 --> 00:26:17,409
<i>♪ ♪</i>

585
00:26:17,410 --> 00:26:19,787
Is this a joke?

586
00:26:19,788 --> 00:26:21,997
I'm not good with jokes.

587
00:26:21,998 --> 00:26:25,626
- Kelly, half of this
is still just symbols.

588
00:26:25,627 --> 00:26:28,420
- You really see
the same thing on both sides?

589
00:26:28,421 --> 00:26:29,755
- It's not word-for-word.

590
00:26:29,756 --> 00:26:32,216
It's--look here.

591
00:26:32,217 --> 00:26:37,179
This says error,
but over here it says mistake.

592
00:26:37,180 --> 00:26:39,306
- You're pointing
to another language.

593
00:26:39,307 --> 00:26:41,725
- I swear, I--
I see it in English.

594
00:26:41,726 --> 00:26:43,560
- That's so weird.

595
00:26:43,561 --> 00:26:46,438
- It wasn't
a reverse subcarrier wave.

596
00:26:46,439 --> 00:26:49,108
[laughs] It was
a two-way subcarrier wave!

597
00:26:49,109 --> 00:26:50,317
- Wait, what?
- Huh?

598
00:26:50,318 --> 00:26:51,860
- When the slab
took English from you,

599
00:26:51,861 --> 00:26:53,278
it also gave you its language,

600
00:26:53,279 --> 00:26:55,781
like the CPU in your brain
is translating for you.

601
00:26:55,782 --> 00:26:57,241
- Gave its language.
OK, wait.

602
00:26:57,242 --> 00:27:01,787
Uh, OK, if you can understand
their language,

603
00:27:01,788 --> 00:27:04,331
we might finally be able to
communicate with our neighbors.

604
00:27:04,332 --> 00:27:06,041
- [chuckles]

605
00:27:06,042 --> 00:27:10,087
- But if I can
translate all this...

606
00:27:10,088 --> 00:27:11,630
why can't I translate that?

607
00:27:11,631 --> 00:27:14,675
<i>[suspenseful music]</i>

608
00:27:14,676 --> 00:27:17,095
<i>♪ ♪</i>

609
00:27:21,641 --> 00:27:24,102
- There is indeed
something in that lake.

610
00:27:27,939 --> 00:27:29,481
- You produced an image?

611
00:27:29,482 --> 00:27:30,607
- Yes.

612
00:27:30,608 --> 00:27:32,693
<i>[device thrumming]</i>

613
00:27:32,694 --> 00:27:33,777
It's a ship.

614
00:27:33,778 --> 00:27:36,488
<i>[device whirring]</i>

615
00:27:36,489 --> 00:27:40,034
<i>[soft suspenseful music]</i>

616
00:27:40,035 --> 00:27:43,370
- It's "EF1."

617
00:27:43,371 --> 00:27:45,956
- Oh, my God.
Are you sure?

618
00:27:45,957 --> 00:27:48,375
<i>♪ ♪</i>

619
00:27:48,376 --> 00:27:52,546
- [sighs]
My son's on that ship.

620
00:27:52,547 --> 00:27:59,346
<i>♪ ♪</i>

621
00:28:05,560 --> 00:28:06,977
- You stole my food rations!

622
00:28:06,978 --> 00:28:09,146
- We don't have
rations anymore!

623
00:28:09,147 --> 00:28:11,899
[thumping and snarling]

624
00:28:11,900 --> 00:28:14,276
<i>[tense music]</i>

625
00:28:14,277 --> 00:28:16,195
- The "Ark 16" infection
is on our--

626
00:28:16,196 --> 00:28:17,488
- He's not Ian.

627
00:28:17,489 --> 00:28:20,824
He's another J6-82 clone
working for Drake,

628
00:28:20,825 --> 00:28:23,035
and I just need
to make him confess.

629
00:28:23,036 --> 00:28:24,203
- Help me, Dr. Kabir!

630
00:28:24,204 --> 00:28:25,204
She's trying to steal
my organs!

631
00:28:25,205 --> 00:28:27,456
- Sharon. Sharon.

632
00:28:27,457 --> 00:28:29,208
I need you to come
with me to med bay.

633
00:28:29,209 --> 00:28:30,542
OK?

634
00:28:30,543 --> 00:28:34,046
<i>[tense music]</i>

635
00:28:34,047 --> 00:28:35,005
- Why?

636
00:28:35,006 --> 00:28:36,965
<i>♪ ♪</i>

637
00:28:36,966 --> 00:28:40,052
- Because you were right.
Drake is after you.

638
00:28:40,053 --> 00:28:44,681
He's after me, too, because I
have Dr. Hall's Gen-3 research.

639
00:28:44,682 --> 00:28:46,850
- We're in this
together, Sanji.

640
00:28:46,851 --> 00:28:48,352
- Yeah.

641
00:28:48,353 --> 00:28:50,646
- First, let me take care
of Drake's agent.

642
00:28:50,647 --> 00:28:52,106
- No! No.

643
00:28:52,107 --> 00:28:56,193
We--we--we might need
to interrogate him later.

644
00:28:56,194 --> 00:29:03,410
<i>♪ ♪</i>

645
00:29:05,745 --> 00:29:07,329
- You're the only one
I can trust, Sanji.

646
00:29:07,330 --> 00:29:11,875
- [grunting]

647
00:29:11,876 --> 00:29:14,962
- You coming?

648
00:29:14,963 --> 00:29:17,464
- [muffled yelling]

649
00:29:17,465 --> 00:29:19,259
Let me up!

650
00:29:20,927 --> 00:29:23,847
<i>[faint beeping]</i>

651
00:29:35,108 --> 00:29:36,525
- OK.

652
00:29:36,526 --> 00:29:40,112
This spore synthesizes
chitin polysaccharide.

653
00:29:40,113 --> 00:29:42,698
At its base, it behaves
a lot like an Earth fungus.

654
00:29:42,699 --> 00:29:45,534
- Are you talking about
the "Ark 16" infection?

655
00:29:45,535 --> 00:29:47,411
- Yeah, but it's
on "Ark 1" now too.

656
00:29:47,412 --> 00:29:50,497
So theoretically,
a strong antifungal

657
00:29:50,498 --> 00:29:52,333
will counteract it immediately.

658
00:29:52,334 --> 00:29:53,751
<i>[tense music]</i>

659
00:29:53,752 --> 00:29:55,002
- Wait.

660
00:29:55,003 --> 00:29:56,754
If it's on "Ark 1,"
why don't you have it?

661
00:29:56,755 --> 00:30:00,758
- Um, because I was late
to the briefing by an hour.

662
00:30:00,759 --> 00:30:02,926
And that's where I would have
first been affected.

663
00:30:02,927 --> 00:30:05,679
- I probably have
less than 15 minutes

664
00:30:05,680 --> 00:30:07,347
until I start
exhibiting symptoms, so--

665
00:30:07,348 --> 00:30:08,682
- Wow.

666
00:30:08,683 --> 00:30:10,142
I'm really glad
you figured this out

667
00:30:10,143 --> 00:30:12,269
before I started
showing symptoms.

668
00:30:12,270 --> 00:30:13,937
- Yeah.

669
00:30:13,938 --> 00:30:15,189
Me too.

670
00:30:15,190 --> 00:30:16,523
[injector clicks]

671
00:30:16,524 --> 00:30:17,691
- Did you just infect me
with the sickness?

672
00:30:17,692 --> 00:30:19,234
- No, no, no, no,
it's the antifungal.

673
00:30:19,235 --> 00:30:22,237
It's the antifungal, which, um,
apparently doesn't work.

674
00:30:22,238 --> 00:30:24,615
<i>♪ ♪</i>

675
00:30:24,616 --> 00:30:26,033
So what kills a fungus?

676
00:30:26,034 --> 00:30:28,786
Damn it, this isn't
my area of expertise.

677
00:30:28,787 --> 00:30:30,829
- Sounds like an Angus thing.

678
00:30:30,830 --> 00:30:33,457
Shame you can't
ask him for help.

679
00:30:33,458 --> 00:30:35,000
- Wait, that is a great idea.

680
00:30:35,001 --> 00:30:37,711
Wait, why can't we ask
Angus for help?

681
00:30:37,712 --> 00:30:39,088
- He knows what he did.

682
00:30:39,089 --> 00:30:41,965
<i>♪ ♪</i>

683
00:30:41,966 --> 00:30:43,550
Did you hear that?

684
00:30:43,551 --> 00:30:45,219
- No.
- Shh!

685
00:30:45,220 --> 00:30:48,222
<i>[tense music]</i>

686
00:30:48,223 --> 00:30:50,140
<i>[WD beeps]</i>

687
00:30:50,141 --> 00:30:51,517
- [groans]

688
00:30:51,518 --> 00:30:52,810
- You never died.

689
00:30:52,811 --> 00:30:54,395
It was all a lie
to cover up your affair.

690
00:30:54,396 --> 00:30:56,230
- You need to defuse
this situation.

691
00:30:56,231 --> 00:30:57,731
- You've lost your bloody mind.

692
00:30:57,732 --> 00:30:59,149
- How is that defusing?

693
00:30:59,150 --> 00:31:01,151
- Least you can do
is be honest with me.

694
00:31:01,152 --> 00:31:02,111
You're in love with Kimi!

695
00:31:02,112 --> 00:31:04,154
- In love with her?
She's--

696
00:31:04,155 --> 00:31:05,781
[sighs]

697
00:31:05,782 --> 00:31:09,326
Sweetheart, I don't know how
to pronounce the woman's name.

698
00:31:09,327 --> 00:31:10,369
- Just tell me the truth.

699
00:31:10,370 --> 00:31:11,412
- The truth?

700
00:31:11,413 --> 00:31:12,746
- Yes!
- Fine. OK.

701
00:31:12,747 --> 00:31:14,164
You want the truth?
Here's the truth.

702
00:31:14,165 --> 00:31:15,499
I'm dead.
Right?

703
00:31:15,500 --> 00:31:16,667
And none of this is real.

704
00:31:16,668 --> 00:31:17,710
- Oh, just be a man
and come clean!

705
00:31:17,711 --> 00:31:19,044
- You need to get
to the med bay.

706
00:31:19,045 --> 00:31:20,170
- You faked your death
so you could be with Kimi!

707
00:31:20,171 --> 00:31:22,006
- Look at the rash--
- Stop it! Stop it!

708
00:31:22,007 --> 00:31:23,340
You're not real.

709
00:31:23,341 --> 00:31:24,758
And you're not real.

710
00:31:24,759 --> 00:31:25,760
OK.

711
00:31:26,928 --> 00:31:28,345
[thud]

712
00:31:28,346 --> 00:31:31,015
- I'm done with you
and your lies!

713
00:31:31,016 --> 00:31:32,224
- Eva to Kimi.

714
00:31:32,225 --> 00:31:33,434
Where are you?

715
00:31:33,435 --> 00:31:36,353
<i>[tense music]</i>

716
00:31:36,354 --> 00:31:39,773
<i>♪ ♪</i>

717
00:31:39,774 --> 00:31:41,859
<i>- Uh, have you tried
antifungal?</i>

718
00:31:41,860 --> 00:31:43,944
- OK, that was
the first thing I tried.

719
00:31:43,945 --> 00:31:46,196
You think I'm a moron,
don't you?

720
00:31:46,197 --> 00:31:48,324
OK. Sorry.

721
00:31:48,325 --> 00:31:49,992
I don't have a lot of time.

722
00:31:49,993 --> 00:31:53,037
<i>[ominous music]</i>

723
00:31:53,038 --> 00:31:55,205
OK, actually,
I don't have any time,

724
00:31:55,206 --> 00:31:56,665
so I need something right now.

725
00:31:56,666 --> 00:31:58,500
<i>- Uh, OK.</i>

726
00:31:58,501 --> 00:32:00,044
<i>Intense UV light
could kill a fungus,</i>

727
00:32:00,045 --> 00:32:01,754
<i>but that'll hurt.</i>

728
00:32:01,755 --> 00:32:03,380
- OK, thanks.
Bye.

729
00:32:03,381 --> 00:32:08,510
<i>♪ ♪</i>

730
00:32:08,511 --> 00:32:11,930
<i>[UV light whirring]</i>

731
00:32:11,931 --> 00:32:13,223
[softly] OK.

732
00:32:13,224 --> 00:32:15,309
<i>♪ ♪</i>

733
00:32:15,310 --> 00:32:18,854
[sizzling]

734
00:32:18,855 --> 00:32:21,482
[screams]

735
00:32:21,483 --> 00:32:22,566
[groans]

736
00:32:22,567 --> 00:32:28,782
<i>♪ ♪</i>

737
00:32:34,287 --> 00:32:36,205
[door opens]

738
00:32:36,206 --> 00:32:39,249
I can work with this.

739
00:32:39,250 --> 00:32:41,001
- I heard a scream.

740
00:32:41,002 --> 00:32:43,295
- I'm all right.

741
00:32:43,296 --> 00:32:44,463
Now...

742
00:32:44,464 --> 00:32:46,548
<i>[UV light whirring]</i>

743
00:32:46,549 --> 00:32:48,133
[sighs]

744
00:32:48,134 --> 00:32:50,719
We need to make sure Drake
isn't putting a tracker on you.

745
00:32:50,720 --> 00:32:53,097
<i>[suspenseful music]</i>

746
00:32:53,098 --> 00:32:55,682
[Sharon screams]

747
00:32:55,683 --> 00:32:59,353
[sizzling]

748
00:32:59,354 --> 00:33:01,605
That was intense.

749
00:33:01,606 --> 00:33:04,316
It felt like everyone
was out to get me.

750
00:33:04,317 --> 00:33:05,651
- How are you feeling now?

751
00:33:05,652 --> 00:33:08,153
- [sighs] Embarrassed.

752
00:33:08,154 --> 00:33:09,488
What did you do?

753
00:33:09,489 --> 00:33:12,032
- UV disinfectant wand.

754
00:33:12,033 --> 00:33:14,493
I turned off the safeties
and cranked it up,

755
00:33:14,494 --> 00:33:17,454
but it's only
a temporary solve.

756
00:33:17,455 --> 00:33:19,873
- 'Cause we don't have time
to use it on the whole crew?

757
00:33:19,874 --> 00:33:22,376
- Well, and the spores are
still in the air.

758
00:33:22,377 --> 00:33:24,253
- So we're already reinfected.

759
00:33:24,254 --> 00:33:25,796
- Probably.

760
00:33:25,797 --> 00:33:27,756
But I have an idea.

761
00:33:27,757 --> 00:33:31,093
There's a small amount of UV
in our lighting system.

762
00:33:31,094 --> 00:33:33,554
Yeah, to combat depression
from lack of sunlight.

763
00:33:33,555 --> 00:33:35,055
- [chuckles softly]

764
00:33:35,056 --> 00:33:37,224
You want to turn "Ark 1" into
a giant disinfectant wand.

765
00:33:37,225 --> 00:33:39,685
- Yeah. If we can figure out
how to recalibrate

766
00:33:39,686 --> 00:33:41,395
the environmental system?

767
00:33:41,396 --> 00:33:42,980
<i>[soft dramatic music]</i>

768
00:33:42,981 --> 00:33:45,858
- Well, I do happen to have an
engineer tied up in my cabin.

769
00:33:45,859 --> 00:33:48,402
<i>[soft dramatic music]</i>

770
00:33:48,403 --> 00:33:50,529
- It's only gonna hurt
a minute, I promise.

771
00:33:50,530 --> 00:33:51,780
But I have to kill
the infection

772
00:33:51,781 --> 00:33:52,990
that's making you sick!
- [groans]

773
00:33:52,991 --> 00:33:54,158
- Almost there, almost there!

774
00:33:54,159 --> 00:33:56,910
All done.

775
00:33:56,911 --> 00:33:58,662
- Space virus?
Really?

776
00:33:58,663 --> 00:34:00,289
- Space fungus.
- Same difference.

777
00:34:00,290 --> 00:34:01,665
- Uh, big difference.

778
00:34:01,666 --> 00:34:03,834
A fungus we can kill by
adjusting the UV in our lights

779
00:34:03,835 --> 00:34:05,085
to disinfectant levels.

780
00:34:05,086 --> 00:34:06,503
- Assuming you know
how to do that.

781
00:34:06,504 --> 00:34:07,504
- Just get me
to the server room.

782
00:34:07,505 --> 00:34:08,714
I'll crank it up
as high as it goes.

783
00:34:08,715 --> 00:34:10,174
- Uh, it's more
complicated than that.

784
00:34:10,175 --> 00:34:13,052
- If you push the UV wavelength
above 222 nanometers,

785
00:34:13,053 --> 00:34:14,636
you will blind the entire ship.

786
00:34:14,637 --> 00:34:15,763
- Ah.

787
00:34:15,764 --> 00:34:17,306
So no pressure then.

788
00:34:17,307 --> 00:34:20,226
<i>[suspenseful music]</i>

789
00:34:22,979 --> 00:34:25,856
<i>[Johann Strauss II's
"The Blue Danube"]</i>

790
00:34:25,857 --> 00:34:29,026
<i>[flowing orchestral waltz]</i>

791
00:34:29,027 --> 00:34:32,905
<i>♪ ♪</i>

792
00:34:32,906 --> 00:34:36,200
[snarling and grunting]

793
00:34:36,201 --> 00:34:38,285
- You're still spying
for the EF!

794
00:34:38,286 --> 00:34:40,954
- You just want
Brice for yourself!

795
00:34:40,955 --> 00:34:44,083
- [gasps]
Oh, god. They're everywhere.

796
00:34:44,084 --> 00:34:45,334
- They're gonna kill
each other.

797
00:34:45,335 --> 00:34:46,335
- We've got this.

798
00:34:46,336 --> 00:34:48,170
<i>♪ ♪</i>

799
00:34:48,171 --> 00:34:49,254
- Stop!

800
00:34:49,255 --> 00:34:50,464
- I'm gonna end
this right now!

801
00:34:50,465 --> 00:34:53,550
<i>[dramatic music]</i>

802
00:34:53,551 --> 00:34:55,844
<i>♪ ♪</i>

803
00:34:55,845 --> 00:34:57,513
- Oh, I'm in
the environmental systems.

804
00:34:57,514 --> 00:34:58,847
Turning off safeties.

805
00:34:58,848 --> 00:35:02,393
<i>♪ ♪</i>

806
00:35:02,394 --> 00:35:04,019
- [yelps]

807
00:35:04,020 --> 00:35:07,773
Uh, shift our output to Far-UVC
and adjust the wavelength.

808
00:35:07,774 --> 00:35:09,024
- 222 nanometers?

809
00:35:09,025 --> 00:35:10,067
- That's the magic number.

810
00:35:10,068 --> 00:35:13,570
- Captain!
She's an EF spy!

811
00:35:13,571 --> 00:35:15,948
- She's sleeping with Brice!
- She's an EF spy!

812
00:35:15,949 --> 00:35:19,868
<i>[dramatic music]</i>

813
00:35:19,869 --> 00:35:21,245
[thuds]
- [shouts]

814
00:35:21,246 --> 00:35:22,913
- Come on, come on.

815
00:35:22,914 --> 00:35:24,707
We're gonna have to go dark
for this to activate.

816
00:35:24,708 --> 00:35:26,709
- Do it!

817
00:35:26,710 --> 00:35:33,216
<i>♪ ♪</i>

818
00:35:36,261 --> 00:35:39,596
No, no, I thought
that would work.

819
00:35:39,597 --> 00:35:41,765
Where--

820
00:35:41,766 --> 00:35:44,935
[all groaning, screaming]

821
00:35:44,936 --> 00:35:46,520
- Yes!
- Oh, my god.

822
00:35:46,521 --> 00:35:47,563
It's working!

823
00:35:47,564 --> 00:35:50,524
[sizzling and screaming]

824
00:35:50,525 --> 00:35:53,569
<i>[dramatic music]</i>

825
00:35:53,570 --> 00:36:00,702
<i>♪ ♪</i>

826
00:36:06,875 --> 00:36:08,834
<i>[electricity thumps]</i>

827
00:36:08,835 --> 00:36:11,795
<i>[peaceful music]</i>

828
00:36:11,796 --> 00:36:15,924
<i>♪ ♪</i>

829
00:36:15,925 --> 00:36:18,761
[crew groaning and coughing]

830
00:36:18,762 --> 00:36:20,679
- Is everyone all right?

831
00:36:20,680 --> 00:36:21,930
- They're fine.

832
00:36:21,931 --> 00:36:23,974
- [sighs]
- Eva.

833
00:36:23,975 --> 00:36:26,727
Uh, I'm so--
- So sorry.

834
00:36:26,728 --> 00:36:28,645
- Are you guys good?
[both sigh]

835
00:36:28,646 --> 00:36:29,647
[indistinct chatter]

836
00:36:29,648 --> 00:36:31,732
<i>♪ ♪</i>

837
00:36:31,733 --> 00:36:33,817
- Are you OK?
Come on.

838
00:36:33,818 --> 00:36:37,113
<i>♪ ♪</i>

839
00:36:39,908 --> 00:36:42,076
- I don't have the words
to thank you, Captain.

840
00:36:42,077 --> 00:36:43,535
- Thank my crew.

841
00:36:43,536 --> 00:36:45,496
They were the ones that
were able to remotely access

842
00:36:45,497 --> 00:36:48,332
your environmental controls
and sterilize your ship.

843
00:36:48,333 --> 00:36:51,710
- We lost 39 souls.

844
00:36:51,711 --> 00:36:53,796
They were good people.

845
00:36:53,797 --> 00:36:57,299
- I have no doubt.

846
00:36:57,300 --> 00:36:58,884
What exactly happened?

847
00:36:58,885 --> 00:37:02,680
- We followed protocol and sent
the scout team to the planet.

848
00:37:02,681 --> 00:37:04,848
They came back
at each other's throats.

849
00:37:04,849 --> 00:37:06,934
- Well, we'll put a beacon
into orbit to warn others

850
00:37:06,935 --> 00:37:10,104
that Deno-197 isn't habitable.

851
00:37:10,105 --> 00:37:12,773
- Thank you.

852
00:37:12,774 --> 00:37:14,692
Where do we go now?

853
00:37:14,693 --> 00:37:18,237
After years in space,
we are still homeless.

854
00:37:18,238 --> 00:37:21,740
- [chuckles] Not quite.

855
00:37:21,741 --> 00:37:24,076
Are you familiar
with the Trappist system?

856
00:37:24,077 --> 00:37:25,452
- No.

857
00:37:25,453 --> 00:37:28,789
- Well, we built a nice colony
there called Homebase 1.

858
00:37:28,790 --> 00:37:30,874
[both chuckle]

859
00:37:30,875 --> 00:37:33,127
<i>♪ ♪</i>

860
00:37:33,128 --> 00:37:36,256
[metallic clanking]

861
00:37:37,966 --> 00:37:39,300
[door clicks]

862
00:37:48,268 --> 00:37:49,769
- [clears throat]

863
00:37:54,190 --> 00:37:56,066
- [sighs]

864
00:37:56,067 --> 00:37:58,736
I am so sorry.

865
00:37:58,737 --> 00:38:01,238
- Stop it.

866
00:38:01,239 --> 00:38:02,990
It was the fungus.

867
00:38:02,991 --> 00:38:05,868
Or the spore or whatever it is

868
00:38:05,869 --> 00:38:07,411
we've decided to call
that space shite.

869
00:38:07,412 --> 00:38:10,831
[both chuckle]

870
00:38:10,832 --> 00:38:14,251
Should we reset?

871
00:38:14,252 --> 00:38:17,588
- Yes, please.
- OK.

872
00:38:17,589 --> 00:38:18,631
[sighs]

873
00:38:20,342 --> 00:38:23,969
- I know
there's no other woman.

874
00:38:23,970 --> 00:38:26,138
- Of course there's not.

875
00:38:26,139 --> 00:38:29,099
<i>[eerie music]</i>

876
00:38:29,100 --> 00:38:33,187
<i>♪ ♪</i>

877
00:38:33,188 --> 00:38:36,316
[indistinct chatter]

878
00:38:37,233 --> 00:38:38,942
- [clears throat]

879
00:38:38,943 --> 00:38:40,361
Permission to join, Captain?

880
00:38:40,362 --> 00:38:43,197
- [laughs]

881
00:38:43,198 --> 00:38:44,698
- Sorry.

882
00:38:44,699 --> 00:38:45,741
Couldn't resist.

883
00:38:45,742 --> 00:38:47,368
- Oh, please don't
make this harder.

884
00:38:47,369 --> 00:38:50,913
I--I didn't mean what I said.

885
00:38:50,914 --> 00:38:52,122
- Stop.

886
00:38:52,123 --> 00:38:53,499
It was just the infection,
all right?

887
00:38:53,500 --> 00:38:54,958
I got a little crazy too.

888
00:38:54,959 --> 00:38:56,252
It's fine.

889
00:39:01,216 --> 00:39:04,093
Can I let you into
a little secret?

890
00:39:04,094 --> 00:39:06,553
Sometimes I get nightmares

891
00:39:06,554 --> 00:39:09,390
about the fact that
I was bred for parts.

892
00:39:09,391 --> 00:39:10,974
- I didn't know that.

893
00:39:10,975 --> 00:39:12,685
- Because I never told you.

894
00:39:12,686 --> 00:39:14,645
And anyway, you kind of
got me worried that you--

895
00:39:14,646 --> 00:39:17,231
- That I'm gonna
steal your liver?

896
00:39:17,232 --> 00:39:19,149
- No, that

897
00:39:19,150 --> 00:39:22,904
the infection might have tapped
into your deepest fears too.

898
00:39:25,281 --> 00:39:28,993
Do you really believe that
no one could ever love you?

899
00:39:28,994 --> 00:39:31,161
- Of course not.

900
00:39:31,162 --> 00:39:34,457
- I mean, you're way too smart
to be that dumb anyway.

901
00:39:37,419 --> 00:39:38,628
Seriously.

902
00:39:42,632 --> 00:39:44,717
Look.

903
00:39:44,718 --> 00:39:48,429
Everyone on this ship
loves you.

904
00:39:48,430 --> 00:39:50,931
Everyone.
Everyone on Homebase loves you.

905
00:39:50,932 --> 00:39:52,434
And I love you.

906
00:39:55,270 --> 00:39:57,521
<i>[soft dramatic music]</i>

907
00:39:57,522 --> 00:39:58,772
I probably should have waited

908
00:39:58,773 --> 00:40:00,107
till we were alone
for that last part.

909
00:40:00,108 --> 00:40:01,942
- I love you too.

910
00:40:01,943 --> 00:40:04,028
<i>[tender music]</i>

911
00:40:04,029 --> 00:40:05,362
[laughter]

912
00:40:05,363 --> 00:40:08,657
<i>♪ ♪</i>

913
00:40:08,658 --> 00:40:10,868
- [chuckling] OK, Captain!

914
00:40:10,869 --> 00:40:13,203
[scattered laughter]

915
00:40:13,204 --> 00:40:15,497
- OK.
- [laughs]

916
00:40:15,498 --> 00:40:17,374
- [mouthing words]

917
00:40:17,375 --> 00:40:19,293
[laughter]

918
00:40:19,294 --> 00:40:20,502
- All right.
Yes, I get it.

919
00:40:20,503 --> 00:40:22,087
I understand now.

920
00:40:22,088 --> 00:40:24,590
- [giggles]

921
00:40:24,591 --> 00:40:26,717
- Hands are sweatin'.
[chuckles]

922
00:40:26,718 --> 00:40:28,927
[sighs]

923
00:40:28,928 --> 00:40:31,972
<i>[suspenseful music]</i>

924
00:40:31,973 --> 00:40:34,892
[birds singing]

925
00:40:34,893 --> 00:40:39,813
<i>♪ ♪</i>

926
00:40:39,814 --> 00:40:43,108
- Zed?

927
00:40:43,109 --> 00:40:45,861
I don't have the words.

928
00:40:45,862 --> 00:40:47,196
- Then don't try.

929
00:40:47,197 --> 00:40:48,489
- I've analyzed the images,

930
00:40:48,490 --> 00:40:52,743
but I can't tell why
"EF1" fell out of the sky.

931
00:40:52,744 --> 00:40:55,913
- I don't know
about your GSA Arks,

932
00:40:55,914 --> 00:40:58,499
but Eastern Federation ships
don't generally

933
00:40:58,500 --> 00:41:00,334
fall out of the sky.

934
00:41:00,335 --> 00:41:02,252
- No, no, of course not.

935
00:41:02,253 --> 00:41:03,253
- It must have been shot down.

936
00:41:03,254 --> 00:41:04,588
- By what?

937
00:41:04,589 --> 00:41:06,715
[approaching footsteps]

938
00:41:06,716 --> 00:41:07,925
- You all need to see this.

939
00:41:07,926 --> 00:41:08,885
It's, um--

940
00:41:10,929 --> 00:41:12,221
It's bad.

941
00:41:12,222 --> 00:41:15,224
<i>[suspenseful music]</i>

942
00:41:15,225 --> 00:41:20,813
<i>♪ ♪</i>

943
00:41:20,814 --> 00:41:23,273
We started a grid search
at the lake shore

944
00:41:23,274 --> 00:41:25,526
and found an area
of disturbed ground.

945
00:41:25,527 --> 00:41:27,069
So we started digging.

946
00:41:27,070 --> 00:41:28,946
- What have you found?

947
00:41:28,947 --> 00:41:31,949
- Bodies.

948
00:41:31,950 --> 00:41:34,743
[indistinct chatter]

949
00:41:34,744 --> 00:41:37,913
<i>[tense somber music]</i>

950
00:41:37,914 --> 00:41:44,838
<i>♪ ♪</i>

951
00:41:45,714 --> 00:41:49,299
- There were survivors.

952
00:41:49,300 --> 00:41:53,930
<i>♪ ♪</i>

953
00:41:58,685 --> 00:42:01,812
<i>[somber music]</i>

954
00:42:01,813 --> 00:42:08,778
<i>♪ ♪</i>

